abstract: >-
  An exact algebraic value rule and attained minimum for the ordinary squared
  Lagrange interpolation integral at every positive number of distinct real nodes.
  The combined formal statement incorporates the credited prior disproof of the
  coefficient-one asymptotic through proved source-correspondence bridges.
keywords:
  - Lagrange interpolation
  - Erdős Problem 1131
  - Hermite matrices
  - exact algebraic minimum
  - formal proof
